{"slug":"count-subsequence-occurrences","title":"How Many Times Is the Word Hidden Inside the Text?","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":744,"tags":["dp","counting","subsequence","string"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Count the ways to build each prefix of the word, letter by letter of the text","body":["In how many ways can the word `t` be obtained from the text `s` by deleting some letters of `s`? Two ways are different if the sets of **positions** kept in `s` are different, even when the resulting letters are the same. For `s = rabbbit` and `t = rabbit` the answer is 3: there are three `b` letters in `s`, and any two of them can be the two `b` letters of `t`. Print the answer modulo 1 000 000 007.","Let `ways(j)` be the number of ways to build the **first `j` letters of `t`** from the part of the text read so far; `ways(0) = 1` (the empty word can be built in one way). Read the text letter by letter. A letter `c = s[i]` can serve as the last letter of the prefix `j` if `t[j] = c`, and then the earlier letters must form the prefix `j - 1` from what was read before: add `ways(j - 1)` to `ways(j)`. Update `j` from the **largest to the smallest**, so that the letter `c` is not used twice in one step.",{"code":"ways = [1] + [0] * m                         # ways[j]: ways to build t[:j]\nfor ch in s:\n    for j in range(m, 0, -1):                # downwards: one text letter, one use\n        if t[j - 1] == ch:\n            ways[j] = (ways[j] + ways[j - 1]) % MOD\nprint(ways[m])"},"The structure is the same as the 0/1 knapsack: every text letter is an \"item\" that is used at most once. The time is O(|s| * |t|), at most one million steps here, and the memory O(|t|). Counting subsequences by \"how many ways for each prefix of the pattern\" also solves many harder counting problems."]},"statement":["Two words `s` and `t` are given. Count the ways to choose positions in `s` such that the letters at these positions, read from left to right, form `t`. Ways with different sets of positions are different. Print the count modulo 1000000007."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the string `s`.","The second line has the string `t`."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of ways modulo 1000000007."],"constraints":["1 <= length of s <= 2000","1 <= length of t <= 500","Both strings consist of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"rabbbit\nrabbit\n","output":"3\n","note":"Any two of the three letters b can be used: 3 ways."},{"input":"abc\nd\n","output":"0\n","note":"The letter d is missing: 0."}],"hints":["Let ways(j) be the number of ways to build the first j letters of t from the text read so far.","A text letter equal to t[j] adds ways(j - 1) to ways(j).","Go through j from the largest to the smallest so that a letter is used only once."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\nt = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n        String t = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["ways(j) is the number of ways to build the first j letters of t from the text read so far; every text letter equal to t[j] adds ways(j - 1) to ways(j), with j going downwards so that each letter is used once. The answer is ways(|t|)."],"complexity":"Time O(|s| * |t|), space O(|t|).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ns = input().strip()\nt = input().strip()\n\nMOD = 10 ** 9 + 7\nm = len(t)\nways = [1] + [0] * m\nfor ch in s:\n    for j in range(m, 0, -1):\n        if t[j - 1] == ch:\n            ways[j] = (ways[j] + ways[j - 1]) % MOD\nprint(ways[m])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string s;\n    cin >> s;\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n\n    const long long MOD = 1000000007;\n    int m = (int)t.size();\n    vector<long long> ways(m + 1, 0);\n    ways[0] = 1;\n    for (char ch : s) {\n        for (int j = m; j >= 1; j--) {\n            if (t[j - 1] == ch) ways[j] = (ways[j] + ways[j - 1]) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ways[m] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String s = next();\n        String t = next();\n\n        final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n        int m = t.length();\n        long[] ways = new long[m + 1];\n        ways[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n            char ch = s.charAt(i);\n            for (int j = m; j >= 1; j--) {\n                if (t.charAt(j - 1) == ch) ways[j] = (ways[j] + ways[j - 1]) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(ways[m]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"rabbbit\nrabbit\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"abc\nd\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"aaa\na\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"aaa\naaaa\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"bbababbaaabbbaaaabaa\nbbbba\n","output":"547\n"},{"input":"cccababbcbccbbcbcabbaabcbaabccaaabaaccacbcbcabacccabbaccbcbbbabacbbbcbaaabcacbcacbcaabccacbaccccaacb\nacaccbacccaaacabbacb\n","output":"162883927\n"},{"input":"\naaabbbabbaabaabbabbbbbaaaabbabbaabbaabbaaaaaabaabbbababbbaaababaaabbaabbbabbbbabbbabaabababaaabbbabb\n","output":"795602731\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"760133385\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"868189750\n"},{"input":"\na\n","output":"2000\n"},{"input":"a\na\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"\ncbaabbaaadddabbcabccaccbabcaddacdacabdbccbdcbdbdbdbddcacbddcddbccdadbdccaaaccabcbdbddadccadacdbdacba\n","output":"737052995\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"162208217\n"},{"input":"\na\n","output":"2000\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"459447475\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"255748234\n"},{"input":"\nb\n","output":"0\n"}]}